# Line endings belong to the repository, not to the machine that cloned it. Git for Windows sets
# `core.autocrlf=true` by default, which checks every file out as CRLF, where Prettier's
# `endOfLine` default is `lf` — so `pnpm run format:check` reported every file in the repository
# as unformatted, including files nobody had touched, and the real failures were lost in the noise.
#
# `text=auto` still normalises to LF in the index the way it always did; `eol=lf` is what makes
# the working tree agree with it, on every platform and whatever `core.autocrlf` is set to.
* text=auto eol=lf
